The rockstar took his wheelchair for a joyride over the audience during his Tuesday (Aug. 19) performance at Portugal&#8217;s Vilar de Mouros festival, where he was performing with his leg still in a cast following a recent dirt-bike accident. In fan-captured videos from the festival, Yungblud yells to his audience, &#8220;I have a broken leg &#8230; and I had two choices: I was either gonna cancel on Portugal, or I was gonna do a shot of Jack Daniels and put a fuckin&#8217; pot on and come rock n&#8217; roll with you!&#8221;

As the rocker is lifted above the crowd while seated in his wheelchair, he belts out the lyrics to &#8220;Fleabag,&#8221; turning a traditional crowd-surf moment into something considerably less conventional. (The track reached No. 15 on Billboard &#8216;s Rock & Alternative Airplay chart in 2022.)

This unexpected stunt is a brave one, considering Yungblud broke his leg just a few weeks ago. Following an accident at the Sturgis Motorcycle Rally on Aug. 9, Yungblud shared photos on Instagram of his leg wrapped in a cast, and promised fans that his live shows will continue despite his injury. He made good on that promise Tuesday, arriving with his injured leg still in a cast.

Afterward, the Grammy winner appeared to take the unconventional crowd-surfing moment in stride. He shared snapshots of the moment on Instagram alongside the humorous caption, &#8220;Good way to break my leg &#8230;&#8221;

Yungblud has one more European festival date on his current schedule: Pukkelpop in Belgium on Aug. 22.
